  "note": "Declared inputs to the dev / held-out split, committed deliberately.\n\n`analysed_before_split` names every case whose criteria were read and discussed during quality work. Knowledge of those cases has already reached the people and agents who edit the skills, so they cannot serve as an independent check and are forced into dev.\n\n`written_blind` names cases authored against a sanitised brief by an author with no access to any measurement result, and never inspected since. They are forced into held-out.\n\nPublishing both lists is the point. This is a discipline split, not an information barrier: the suite is public, so anyone can read a held-out case. What the split commits to is not secrecy but restraint — not iterating against these cases — and an undisclosed split is indistinguishable from a convenient one.",
